From 340631d1648be435e1bc354bf4aa4150aec41603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup.py: map riscv64 to manylinux_2_39_riscv64 in the wheel
 platform tag

genericpy_bdist_wheel.get_tag() only special-cases linux_x86_64 and
linux_aarch64 (both mapped to the manylinux2014 policy this project
targets on those architectures). riscv64 falls through unmapped, so a
CIBUILDWHEEL=1 build on linux_riscv64 would otherwise ship a wheel
tagged plain 'linux_riscv64', which pip rejects as non-manylinux.

manylinux2014 predates riscv64 entirely (PEP 599 has no riscv64
mapping), so riscv64 is tagged against manylinux_2_39 instead -- the
oldest manylinux policy with a riscv64 image, matching the
quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64 container used to build it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [cbcbox's own CI (wheel.yml) does not build for riscv64 at all -- no GitHub-hosted riscv64 runner exists -- so this mapping has no upstream job to exercise it]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 15d501d..a8c01e4 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ class genericpy_bdist_wheel(_bdist_wheel):
                 plat = "manylinux2014_x86_64"
             elif plat == "linux_aarch64":
                 plat = "manylinux2014_aarch64"
+            elif plat == "linux_riscv64":
+                plat = "manylinux_2_39_riscv64"
         return python, abi, plat
 
 
